WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:06.040
Modern horror movies often go overlooked,
but from time to time, a spectacularly terrifying

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.210
film takes the public by storm.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.590
Perhaps 2017 is the year that happens again,
and any number of the following horror movies

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.590
could do it.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.070
Here are all of the horror movies that will
blow everyone away in 2017.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.140
Split

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.449
This could be the year that M. Night Shyamalan's
career experiences a renaissance, and after

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:26.560
flops like The Last Airbender, he really needs
it.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.470
His latest film, Split, is loosely inspired
by the true story of Billy Milligan, the first

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.520
person to be acquitted of a major crime because
of his multiple personality disorder.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.320
Filmmakers have been trying to bring Milligan's
story to life on the big screen for years,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.500
and now Shyamalan is making it happen.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.160
James McAvoy, still bald from X-Men: Apocalypse,
stars as Kevin, who suffers from dissociative

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.120
identity disorder, in what could be a long
awaited return to form for Shyamalan.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.890
Resident Evil: The Final Chapter

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.790
Milla Jovovich is back for the long-awaited,
final installment in the Resident Evil movie

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.790
series.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:05.530
Despite falling victim to the video game movie
curse, the franchise continues to turn a profit

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.009
and will likely do so again with Resident
Evil: The Final Chapter.

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:13.670
In this ultimate installment, releasing in
late January, Alice and her band of survivors

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.060
will make their final stand against the Umbrella
Corporation and the undead in the dreaded

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.130
Raccoon City.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.969
We're five movies and over twenty games deep,
so why stop now?

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:25.259
Rings

00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:27.990
Over a decade after The Ring Two was released
in theaters…

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.640
"Mommy!"

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.080
"I'm not your ----ing mommy!"

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:36.750
….Paramount is bringing it back for a third
installment, simply titled Rings, which takes

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.149
place 13 years after the events of the first
movie.

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:44.700
Since VHS isn't really a thing anymore, it's
now a digital video that'll kill you in seven

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.619
days, which is pretty much the worst computer
virus ever.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:49.810
"Do you want to destroy humans?

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.810
Please say no."

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.679
"Ok, I will destroy humans."

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.579
"Noo I take it back!

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:56.940
Don't destroy humans."

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.630
The twist?

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.659
There's a part of the deadly video that no
one's seen until now, so expect completely

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:07.049
new levels of chaos and even more drippy horror
children on February 3rd.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:08.640
A Cure for Wellness

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.950
You might not expect a horror movie from the
guy who directed Rango, but Gore Verbinski

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.910
is going back to his horror roots with his
next film, A Cure for Wellness.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:21.390
On February 17th, he's turning the tables
and making a psychological horror starring

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.560
Dane DeHaan and the naturally terrifying Mia
Goth.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.010
The film follows DeHaan's Mr. Lockhart as
he attempts to retrieve his company's CEO

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.780
and escape from a mysterious wellness center
in the Swiss Alps.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.060
Of course, this isn't a feel-good film about
getting one's groove back, and the wellness

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.120
center doesn't really have its customers'
best interests at heart, so psychological

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.450
terror ensues.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.450
Get Out

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:48.740
"Get out."

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.260
"Sorry man."

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:50.740
"Get out!"

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.400
"Yo!"

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.510
"Aaahhh!"

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.320
Marking the directorial debut of comedian
Jordan Peele, best known for Comedy Central's

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.500
Key &amp; Peele, Get Out follows an interracial
couple as they visit a town where black residents

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.320
have begun to go missing.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.531
Starring Daniel Kaluuya, Allison Williams,
Catherine Keener, and Erika Alexander, Get

00:03:09.531 --> 00:03:14.120
Out is being produced by Blumhouse Productions,
who rarely makes bad horror movies.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:19.040
Just look at their slate: Paranormal Activity,
Insidious, The Purge, and Sinister are just

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.750
some of their iconic films.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.930
Moving from comedy acting to horror directing
is a big leap, but early buzz surrounding

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.330
this film's February 24th release is all positive.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.590
Personal Shopper

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:35.060
Though she'll always be best known as Twilight's
Bella Swan, Kristen Stewart continues to make

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.280
a name for herself in numerous independent
films.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.730
Next up is the French-made psychological thriller
Personal Shopper, which follows Stewart as

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.240
Maureen, who's employed as a personal shopper
for a German model.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.240
The twist?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.750
When she's not buying stuff for pretty people,
she's trying to contact her dead brother,

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.750
Lewis.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.600
Where those two things meet is anyone's guess,
but surprisingly, the film earned the Best

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.010
Director award at the 2016 Cannes Film Festival.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.760
The film gets a wide release on March 10th.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.819
Alien: Covenant

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:08.940
Featuring the return of Michael Fassbender,
and featuring Katherine Waterston, Billy Crudup,

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.050
and Danny McBride, director Ridley Scott is
finally bringing his Prometheus sequel, Alien:

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.590
Covenant, to theaters this year.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:21.560
This isn't to be confused with a new Alien
film, stuck in development hell since 2002

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.020
and directed by Neill Blomkamp, which is supposedly
following later.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.600
We're still in pre-Alien continuity here.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.960
Although Scott's original idea was to explore
the mysteries left unanswered in Prometheus

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.620
with Noomi Rapace returning as Elizabeth Shaw,
things have taken a different turn.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.340
Instead of directly following the events of
Prometheus, Alien: Covenant will follow a

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:45.350
new crew, aboard a new ship, whose path will
intersect with the survivors of the Prometheus.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.310
Meet the new xenomorphs on May 19th.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.310
The Mummy

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:53.470
Even Universal Pictures is climbing aboard
the cinematic universe train.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:56.991
Since they don't have a catalog of comic book
properties they can sift through, they're

00:04:56.991 --> 00:05:01.090
mounting their shared universe around the
iconic monsters that made them a worldwide

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.090
brand, beginning with Alex Kurtzman's The
Mummy on June 9th.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:10.150
Starring Tom Cruise, Sofia Boutella, and Russell
Crowe as Dr. Henry Jekyll, The Mummy ignores

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:14.720
the delightful campiness of Brendan Fraser's
previous Mummy trilogy, and instead brings

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.530
the film back to its horror roots.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:20.630
The new film also takes the franchise in a
new direction by setting it in the present

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.900
day and featuring a new mummy.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.389
Taking down Imhotep three times was more than
enough.

00:05:26.389 --> 00:05:28.130
Amityville: The Awakening

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:33.880
The June 30th release of Franck Khalfoun's
Amityville: The Awakening will mark the 18th

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.020
movie based on the haunted house since the
series' inception in 1979.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:42.720
Each installment in the Amityville franchise
just adds to the weird continuity nightmare,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.180
which has been plagued with prequels, pre-sequels,
and an occasional lawsuit.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:52.020
(Hilariously bad chainsaw scene)

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.070
You probably know what to expect with the
new Amityville chapter: a single mother and

00:05:56.070 --> 00:06:02.080
her three kids unknowingly move into the infamous
112 Ocean Avenue house, and terror ensues.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.080
Worst realtor ever.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.690
You should always put 'bleeding walls' in
the listing.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.680
Some people might even like that kinda thing!

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.950
"Make the walls bleed!"

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:09.950
"No."

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.110
"Hey man we own you, let's see some blood!"

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.360
"I don't have to entertain you!"

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:14.960
"Come on man!

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:15.520
Do it!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.300
Do the blood thing!

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:16.980
Come on, do it!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:17.480
do it!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:17.980
do it!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.440
Annabelle 2

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:26.120
In 2013, The Conjuring surprised audiences
by effectively reinventing age-old scare tactics,

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.980
and was popular enough to warrant a spin-off.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:33.910
That movie, Annabelle, focused on the origins
of the terror doll made famous by the original.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.680
Now, Annabelle is becoming its own horror
series, because honestly, she's pretty freakin'

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.180
scary.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:42.260
"Stop!

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:43.640
----!"

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:47.880
The new installment follows a nun and a group
of young girls who move into a dollmaker's

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.890
home.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.480
And because it's a horror film, it's the same
hoouse in which the dollmaker's daughter died

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.740
20 years prior.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:07:01.050
Annabelle finds a fresh set of new victims
on August 11th.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.050
IT

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.370
Hollywood loves adapting Stephen King's works.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:09.400
A miniseries based on the novel IT aired on
television in 1990, starring Tim Curry as

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.449
Pennywise.

00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:15.880
But that just wasn't enough for fans of nightmare
clowns.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:20.900
A cinematic version of IT is due to hit theaters
on September 8th, but because of production

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:26.230
challenges and a change in director, the production's
original star, Will Poulter, will no longer

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.610
be playing Pennywise.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.960
His replacement, Bill Skarsgard, seems pretty
terrifying, but he's got some big, Tim Curry-sized

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.450
shoes to fill.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:35.980
"Excuse me sir!

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.610
Do you have Prince Albert in a can?

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:39.610
You do?!

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.220
Well ya better let the poor guy out!

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.040
Woo ha!

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:42.620
Woo ha!

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.300
Woo ha!"

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.110
Flatliners

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.919
Years before Joel Schumacher destroyed Batman...

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:57.940
...he brought Peter Filardi's science fiction
horror film, Flatliners, to the silver screen.

00:07:57.949 --> 00:08:02.550
The film follows five medical students as
they voluntarily subject themselves to near-death

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.830
experiences in order to discover what lies
in the afterlife.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:12.680
Now, 27 years later, a sequel is in the works,
also titled Flatliners, starring Ellen Page,

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:17.860
Diego Luna, and Nina Dobrev, with Kiefer Sutherland
returning from the original movie.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:22.069
A plot summary hasn't been released yet, but
you can expect a whole lot of almost dying

00:08:22.069 --> 00:08:27.110
— and maybe a little bit of actual dying
too — on September 29th.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.310
Friday the 13th

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:34.300
Warner Bros. originally commissioned a Friday
the 13th sequel in 2009, but the studio canceled

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:38.700
the project before relinquishing the rights
to Paramount Pictures so they could co-produce

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.240
Christopher Nolan's Interstellar.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.190
Fans were disappointed, but Paramount immediately
began working on their own Friday the 13th

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.190
movie.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:50.240
According to reports, the new film will be
an origin story, featuring the return of Jason's

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:55.230
mother… and was reportedly almost some deranged
version of Dazed and Confused meets Jason.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:56.899
As if this wasn't creepy enough.

00:08:56.899 --> 00:09:00.220
"That's what I love about these high school
girls man.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:06.000
I get older, they stay the same age ahahaha."

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:10.350
What's more, this will be the 13th installment
in the Friday the 13th franchise, which will

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.700
also release on Friday the 13th this October.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.710
Insidious: Chapter 4

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:21.310
James Wan is truly the modern master of horror,
having created the Saw, Conjuring, and Insidious

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.310
franchises.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:27.260
Today, he's directing things like Furious
7 and DC's upcoming Aquaman film.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:33.399
But despite his exit from the Insidious franchise,
it continues to prosper, so much that FilmDistrict

00:09:33.399 --> 00:09:38.990
ordered a fourth installment to be directed
by Adam Robitel and written by franchise co-creator

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.090
Leigh Whannell.

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:45.480
Not much is known about the film at this time,
except for its strategic October release date.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.430
Saw: Legacy

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:52.770
When the Saw franchise began in 2004, one
installment was released every year until

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.870
2010…. and then nothing.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.330
Now, seven years later, it's back for one
last chapter with Saw: Legacy, directed by

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.550
the Spierig Brothers.

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:03.650
So, why are they bringing Saw back after all
these years?

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:08.270
The filmmakers originally intended Saw 3D
to be the final installment in the long-running

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.270
franchise.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:14.209
However, when Saw 6 underperformed at the
box office, Lionsgate approved one more movie,

00:10:14.209 --> 00:10:18.580
which hindered the filmmakers' plans and left
the franchise with an unsatisfactory twist

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.650
and more questions than answers.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:26.150
Saw: Legacy, releasing on October 27th, will
hopefully answer some of those lingering mysteries,

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.670
as well as reinvent the franchise.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.160
Thanks for watching!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.900
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.320
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

